<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/paperwork-review.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/paperwork-review-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/paperwork-review.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal-services/">Services</a></li><li aria-current="page">Neutral Umpire Services</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Appraisal service</p><h1>Neutral Umpire Services for Appraisal Panels</h1><p class="lede">When two appraisers can’t settle every item, a neutral umpire decides. We serve as umpire on residential and commercial panels where we have no role on either side.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-y" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Neutral decision-maker</dd></div><div><dt>Appointed by</dt><dd>Appraisers or court</dd></div><div><dt>Conflicts</dt><dd>Disclosed up front</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>What an umpire does</h2>
<p>An umpire is the third member of an appraisal panel. The two appraisers select the umpire, or a court appoints one if they can’t agree. The umpire reviews the items the appraisers couldn’t resolve and decides them. An award signed by the umpire and either appraiser sets the amount of loss.</p>
<h2>How we serve as umpire</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Conflict check first.</strong> We disclose any prior work with either appraiser, the insurer or the property owner before accepting.</li>
<li><strong>Clear ground rules.</strong> We set out how submissions, inspections and communication will work, in writing.</li>
<li><strong>Evidence-based decisions.</strong> We inspect when useful and decide each item on the measurements, photos and pricing presented.</li>
<li><strong>Clean award forms.</strong> Awards are itemized by coverage with replacement cost, depreciation and actual cash value spelled out.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Independence matters</h2>
<p>We never serve as umpire on a claim where we acted as appraiser or reviewed the estimate for either side. When we serve as umpire, we do not communicate with one side without the other. Neutrality is what makes an award hold up.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Appointment by court</b>Most Washington policies say that if the appraisers can’t agree on an umpire within a set time, either party may ask a court of record in the county where the property is located to appoint one. We accept court appointments as well as appointments by agreement.</div>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who pays the umpire?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Policies usually split umpire fees equally between the insured and the insurer. Our fee is set out in writing before we start.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can one side contact the umpire directly?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>We don’t hold one-sided conversations about the merits. Communication goes to both appraisers.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you serve as umpire outside Washington?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>This practice focuses on Washington properties, where we know local pricing and policy practice best.</p></div></details></div><h2>Related services</h2><div class="cards3 tight"><a class="pcard rv" href="/insurance-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consultation-table.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-table-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation-table.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Related service</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Appraisal Clause Representation</h3><span class="pcard-p">We act as the appraiser you name once either side demands a